WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.329 --> 00:00:04.770
Those who have studied the various anomalies
contained by the SCP Foundation know that

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:07.480
this world has quite a lot to fear.

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:13.080
Enormous world-devouring monsters that thrive
on an endless stream of hate, seemingly innocuous

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:18.230
statues waiting to snap your neck the second
your turn your back, and a shark-eyed old

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:23.130
man with the power to reach through solid
concrete, grab hold of your with his rotting

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:27.119
hands, and drag you into his own personal
hell.

00:00:27.119 --> 00:00:32.880
SCP-106 can pop into our world whenever he
wants, but like many of the most efficient

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:38.100
predators, he has his own designated lair,
a pocket dimension where he can pull his prey

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:43.840
and trap them in a horrifying game of cat
and mouse that only ever ends one way: in

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:46.480
a painful, prolonged end.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:52.400
We all know what SCP-106 uses his pocket dimension
for, but what if some of the other anomalies

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:55.910
at the Foundation had a pocket dimension of
their very own?

00:00:55.910 --> 00:01:01.989
A tiny, parallel reality that they could shape
in their image, use for whatever they wanted?

00:01:01.989 --> 00:01:03.620
What might that look like?

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:08.630
A special team of SCP Foundation operatives
were tasked with conducting an experiment,

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:13.259
using an elaborate computer system to run
simulations and see what different anomalies

00:01:13.259 --> 00:01:18.759
might do with their pocket dimensions, should
the opportunity ever arise.

00:01:18.759 --> 00:01:21.799
Stranger things have certainly happened at
the SCP Foundation.

00:01:21.799 --> 00:01:26.829
So, they prepared a list of anomalies that
presented the most potential for interesting

00:01:26.829 --> 00:01:29.079
findings, and fired up the simulation.

00:01:29.079 --> 00:01:36.630
For the very first subject, they selected
an anomaly who was also a colleague: Dr. Bright,

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:38.030
and SCP-963.

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:42.320
The monitor attached to the computer running
the simulation showed a curious, surprising

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:43.320
picture.

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:47.060
There was a door, with one sign: "Bright Council
Meeting Inside."

00:01:47.060 --> 00:01:51.110
Past the door was a long conference table
packed to the brim with different attendees.

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:58.090
There were guards, D-Class, scientists, men
and women, all wearing the trademark anomalous

00:01:58.090 --> 00:01:59.090
amulet.

00:01:59.090 --> 00:02:04.079
It was every single incarnation of the Doctor
himself, all talking over each other with

00:02:04.079 --> 00:02:06.110
great enthusiasm.

00:02:06.110 --> 00:02:10.459
At the head of the table there was a monitor,
depicting the current incarnation of Dr. Bright

00:02:10.459 --> 00:02:13.790
going about his daily life on a live video
feed.

00:02:13.790 --> 00:02:19.240
All of the many, many Dr. Brights were instructing
him, giving him advice and guidance on every

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:21.300
impulsive decision.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:26.580
Some Dr. Brights were brandishing pies, others
chainsaws, and others were drawing schematics

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:28.860
for laser guns and catapults.

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:34.630
The Council of Brights was working together,
devising pranks, schemes, and general tomfoolery.

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:38.569
The research team all agreed that Dr. Bright
could never learn about this simulation result,

00:02:38.569 --> 00:02:41.319
lest he try to recreate it himself.

00:02:41.319 --> 00:02:48.580
Next, they input details about SCP-5094, Ms.
J's Whiz Kidz Schoolhouse, the anomalous computer

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:52.010
program capable of teaching anyone about any
subject.

00:02:52.010 --> 00:02:57.630
With a triumphant beep, the computer announced
that it had rendered a simulation of Ms. J's

00:02:57.630 --> 00:02:59.550
pocket dimension might be.

00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:05.010
It was a classroom, decorated in bright colors
and cutouts of various numbers and letters.

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:09.049
On the wall, motivational portraits were displayed
including kittens grabbing on to the rungs

00:03:09.049 --> 00:03:11.550
of a ladder with the slogan: "Hang in there!"

00:03:11.550 --> 00:03:16.260
There were bookshelves all along the walls,
filled to the brim with books.

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:21.100
At the chalkboard, a three-dimensional version
of Ms. J herself was standing with her signature

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:25.390
ponytail and bright green vest, piece of chalk
in her hand.

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:30.310
The desks were all empty, but she had a chipper
smile on her face, and was waiting for students

00:03:30.310 --> 00:03:32.830
to come in and learn any minute.

00:03:32.830 --> 00:03:35.730
On the board, she had written: "Welcome, class!"

00:03:35.730 --> 00:03:40.610
Next, they chose an entity whose inner life
was a bit more difficult to discern, whose

00:03:40.610 --> 00:03:44.450
motivations, though seemingly straightforward,
were perplexing.

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:50.360
SCP-049, the Plague Doctor, forever in pursuit
of curing a Pestilence that he could not get

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:56.409
the Foundation to understand, creating lifeless
zombies whenever he attempted to treat a patient.

00:03:56.409 --> 00:04:00.870
Where would this inscrutable Doctor disappear
to, if he only could?

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:03.049
What would his hideaway be?

00:04:03.049 --> 00:04:07.890
The simulation rendered a sterile laboratory
environment, no real surprise given his proclivity

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:09.629
for medical science.

00:04:09.629 --> 00:04:12.599
There were stainless steel tables and instruments.

00:04:12.599 --> 00:04:17.470
The Plague Doctor stood in the fully outfitted
lab, going about his work as he always did,

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:20.220
with no one to interrupt or disturb him.

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:25.190
On a desk in the corner sat a pile of medical
texts, a vase filled with lavender flowers

00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:29.500
in fresh water, and a generous glass of rich
red wine.

00:04:29.500 --> 00:04:32.600
There was everything here that he could possibly
need.

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:36.780
What about a pocket dimension for an entity
that already had everything it could possibly

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:37.780
want?

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:44.930
Something so content, so happy with its everyday
life, that it had no need or desire to escape?

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:51.210
SCP-999 lived as a pampered pet, a sort of
Foundation mascot, with its every wish for

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:53.750
tasty treats or playtime met.

00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:58.669
Still, they input the Tickle Monster's information
into the simulation, to see what it might

00:04:58.669 --> 00:04:59.669
come up with.

00:04:59.669 --> 00:05:03.500
What it rendered looked like something out
of Willy Wonka and the Chocolate Factory.

00:05:03.500 --> 00:05:09.390
It was a wide-open field beneath a bright
blue sky filled with sunlight and fluffy white

00:05:09.390 --> 00:05:10.390
clouds.

00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:15.360
The landscape, however, was not the greenery
and nature one might expect to see, but instead

00:05:15.360 --> 00:05:18.580
was made up entirely of candy and other sweets.

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:23.490
Boulders made of toffee, a lake of melted
chocolate, lollipop trees, and cotton candy

00:05:23.490 --> 00:05:26.260
bushes as far as the eye could see.

00:05:26.260 --> 00:05:30.880
Nestled within the candy landscape was an
elaborate playground, more of an amusement

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:34.430
park than the usual row of swings and a plastic
slide.

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:40.509
There was a miniature Ferris wheel, a ball
pit, and an obstacle course that SCP-999 could

00:05:40.509 --> 00:05:42.550
bounce around and navigate.

00:05:42.550 --> 00:05:46.620
Every simple, childlike joy was present in
this place.

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:48.880
Pure sweetness, happiness, and light.

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:54.470
For a creature as good as SCP-999, they would
expect nothing less.

00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:59.580
Next up was the deadly statue that moved only
when out of sight, SCP-173.

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:04.430
It took the researchers a moment to understand
what they were seeing when they took a look

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:09.680
at its dimension, at first they thought that
perhaps the simulation had somehow crashed.

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:12.520
After all, they were looking at a pitch-black
screen.

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:14.600
Then, they realized.

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:18.130
They were seeing what its dimension would
look like after all.

00:06:18.130 --> 00:06:24.970
The perfect place for SCP-173 to retreat to
would be somewhere cloaked in absolute darkness,

00:06:24.970 --> 00:06:29.490
where no one could keep an eye on the statue
and stop it from moving as it pleased.

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:34.590
Here, it would be free to hunt and take lives
as much as it wanted, keeping unsuspecting

00:06:34.590 --> 00:06:39.630
humans in suspense as they waited for the
sound of grinding stone to betray that the

00:06:39.630 --> 00:06:41.280
end was near.

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:46.410
The researchers all shuddered, and glanced
over their shoulders, just in case.

00:06:46.410 --> 00:06:50.490
Since they were already feeling unsettled,
they decided to take it one step further and

00:06:50.490 --> 00:06:54.650
see what SCP-682 might create for itself.

00:06:54.650 --> 00:06:57.440
What could be home for the creature that hates
everything?

00:06:57.440 --> 00:07:02.690
They were horrified to see a bleak, stony
landscape where the massive reptile was devouring

00:07:02.690 --> 00:07:04.449
everything in sight.

00:07:04.449 --> 00:07:10.970
Humans, plants, animals, none were safe from
being snapped up in its deadly jaws.

00:07:10.970 --> 00:07:12.690
That wasn't the worst of it, though.

00:07:12.690 --> 00:07:18.630
When it had finished consuming everything,
SCP-682 opened its mouth and coughed all of

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:22.800
its victims back up, miraculously resurrected
and unharmed.

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:29.330
Then, it began to do it all over again, ripping,
tearing, and clawing at all the living things

00:07:29.330 --> 00:07:32.879
around it in an endless cycle of despair.

00:07:32.879 --> 00:07:36.770
One researcher began to feel sick, and had
to flee the room.

00:07:36.770 --> 00:07:41.490
The rest pressed on, if a bit paler than they
had been moments before.

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:45.830
Since the vibes in the room were already as
bad as they could possibly get, one researcher

00:07:45.830 --> 00:07:51.479
suggested they keep the momentum going and
try out another highly hostile anomaly: the

00:07:51.479 --> 00:07:56.310
possessive mask itself, SCP-035.

00:07:56.310 --> 00:08:01.180
What sort of cursed reality could the simulation
come up with for the malicious mask, a being

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:07.600
that, though it couldn't move on its own,
seemed to radiate an almost unstoppable evil?

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:12.550
The monitor showed a rendering of an ornately
decorated castle with a Medieval European

00:08:12.550 --> 00:08:19.150
sensibility: gold decor and rich red velvet
curtains, dots of black and red like blood,

00:08:19.150 --> 00:08:21.490
and black goo on everything.

00:08:21.490 --> 00:08:26.470
On the walls, elaborate tapestries were hung
depicting the traditional comedy and tragedy

00:08:26.470 --> 00:08:30.000
masks that SCP-035 resembled.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:35.120
There was a stained glass window toward the
back of the room, depicting SCP-035, with

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:41.529
a full human body, sitting atop a golden throne,
a crown on its head.

00:08:41.529 --> 00:08:47.029
In the very center of the room, there was
SCP-035, in a position matching the stained

00:08:47.029 --> 00:08:48.029
glass window.

00:08:48.029 --> 00:08:54.250
At its feet, dozens of people dressed in rags
were kneeling in supplication to their ruler.

00:08:54.250 --> 00:08:56.500
The mask was smiling.

00:08:56.500 --> 00:09:00.890
Of course, that awful thing would want to
make itself the king of its own private castle,

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:03.430
forcing others to serve it every whim.

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:07.279
Time to shift gears to something completely
different.

00:09:07.279 --> 00:09:10.760
SCP-2662, also known as Cthulhu.

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:16.270
Despite the creature's intimidating appearance,
he was overall a relatively polite being.

00:09:16.270 --> 00:09:19.740
What would his chosen sanctuary look like?

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:26.510
SCP-2662's simulated pocket dimension was
a far cry from the luxury of SCP-035's.

00:09:26.510 --> 00:09:30.480
There were no riches here, no opulent displays
of wealth and power.

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:31.680
It was the opposite.

00:09:31.680 --> 00:09:37.430
The room depicted resembled a standard studio
apartment with a bed, a couch, a television,

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:38.910
and a kitchenette.

00:09:38.910 --> 00:09:43.190
Every up-to-date game console - and some that
didn't exist yet - could be seen throughout

00:09:43.190 --> 00:09:49.380
the room, and posters for various video games
and action and sci-fi movies adorned the walls.

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:53.529
There were stacks and stacks of games ready
to be played, as well as an extra-large bean

00:09:53.529 --> 00:09:57.570
bag chair positioned directly in front of
the TV screen.

00:09:57.570 --> 00:10:01.880
There, SCP-2662 sat, gaming happily.

00:10:01.880 --> 00:10:05.580
The room had no windows, and no visible door
either.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:10.110
No way for strangers to intrude on his peaceful
private leisure time.

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:14.540
Up next on the list was SCP-953, the Polymorphic
Humanoid.

00:10:14.540 --> 00:10:19.760
But when the simulation rendered her pocket
dimension, she was nowhere to be seen.

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:24.320
There was a beautiful landscape, like something
out of a painting, of what appeared to be

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:27.279
an idyllic location in rural Korea.

00:10:27.279 --> 00:10:32.410
There was vibrant green grass, a light blue
sky dotted with delicate wisps of cloud, and

00:10:32.410 --> 00:10:34.150
a clear trickling stream.

00:10:34.150 --> 00:10:39.240
There was a man lying by the stream, basking
in the sunlight, though he didn't look like

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:41.709
any anomaly the research team recognized.

00:10:41.709 --> 00:10:46.570
They were checking him for the telltale fox
ears or tail that indicated a shapeshifted

00:10:46.570 --> 00:10:52.139
SCP-953, when suddenly a figure emerged from
the water.

00:10:52.139 --> 00:10:57.769
A woman with long dark hair, wearing a white
dress, and with those oh-so-familiar ears

00:10:57.769 --> 00:10:59.649
poking out from her scalp.

00:10:59.649 --> 00:11:03.520
She stretched her sharp claws wide, and snapped
her fingers.

00:11:03.520 --> 00:11:05.570
Suddenly, the landscape changed.

00:11:05.570 --> 00:11:10.400
The sky went dark, the clouds replaced with
fox's eyes glaring down from the heavens,

00:11:10.400 --> 00:11:16.300
the stream flowed red with blood, and the
grass became a carpet of gnarled orange fur.

00:11:16.300 --> 00:11:21.730
The man scrambled to his feet in a desperate
bid for escape, but SCP-953 jumped on him

00:11:21.730 --> 00:11:27.279
before he could take so much as a step away
from her, and began to torture him gleefully.

00:11:27.279 --> 00:11:30.380
The screen went red, as if with blood.

00:11:30.380 --> 00:11:35.100
The Researchers definitely needed a palate
cleanser after that nightmarish vision, so

00:11:35.100 --> 00:11:39.680
they selected a much more wholesome entity
from the list for the next round.

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:46.390
SCP-2295, the Patchwork Bear that so deeply
wanted to heal the world and help the sick

00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:47.480
and hurting.

00:11:47.480 --> 00:11:52.209
Its simulated dimension resembled an ordinary
doctor's office waiting room, with chairs,

00:11:52.209 --> 00:11:56.889
a check-in desk, and some toys and books for
bored patients of all ages.

00:11:56.889 --> 00:12:01.730
There was one difference, however: everything
in the room was made from scrap fabric and

00:12:01.730 --> 00:12:07.389
yarn, materials the bear could use to patch
a potentially infinite number of troubles.

00:12:07.389 --> 00:12:11.680
This was a place where the bear could bring
anyone in need of its help, and treat them

00:12:11.680 --> 00:12:13.199
to the best of its ability.

00:12:13.199 --> 00:12:18.220
But what about an anomaly that was not sentient,
or at the very least, one whose sentience

00:12:18.220 --> 00:12:20.160
was very much up for debate?

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:24.699
The team selected SCP-914 for the next simulation.

00:12:24.699 --> 00:12:30.699
Inputting the details of SCP-914, or the Clockworks,
resulted in an image of a small factory with

00:12:30.699 --> 00:12:32.010
large metal doors.

00:12:32.010 --> 00:12:37.750
Inside, all manner of unidentifiable machinery
worked in tandem to rearrange and reconfigure

00:12:37.750 --> 00:12:39.459
various items.

00:12:39.459 --> 00:12:43.240
There were different conveyor belts, each
marked according to one of the Clockworks'

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:48.370
settings: Coarse, Rough, 1:1, Fine, and Very
Fine.

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:53.100
Perhaps, one researcher posited, this particular
pocket dimension was not theoretical at all.

00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:57.529
Maybe this was where items went when they
disappeared into the machine's intake booth?

00:12:57.529 --> 00:13:03.649
Then again, who could be certain how exactly
an item like SCP-914 really worked?

00:13:03.649 --> 00:13:07.050
Next was SCP-073, Cain.

00:13:07.050 --> 00:13:12.389
In his dimension, the world of his own making,
he strolled through a dense forest, the vegetation

00:13:12.389 --> 00:13:16.339
thriving all around him where it would have
ordinarily withered and died.

00:13:16.339 --> 00:13:21.250
He plucked an apple off of a tree, and took
a bite.

00:13:21.250 --> 00:13:25.370
SCP-529, Josie the Half Cat, romped through
a playroom that could only be described as

00:13:25.370 --> 00:13:26.779
"cat heaven."

00:13:26.779 --> 00:13:31.899
Scratching posts, fish and chicken treats,
balls of yarn, everything a feline friend

00:13:31.899 --> 00:13:33.610
could ever desire.

00:13:33.610 --> 00:13:37.331
One researcher wiped a tear from her eye,
and when her colleagues questioned it, she

00:13:37.331 --> 00:13:40.380
just replied, "I really like cats, okay?!"

00:13:40.380 --> 00:13:45.850
In a subject change, another Researcher suggested
trying a sort of "before and after" experiment

00:13:45.850 --> 00:13:47.440
with the simulation.

00:13:47.440 --> 00:13:51.529
They would see what sort of pocket dimension
might be generated by an anomaly before a

00:13:51.529 --> 00:13:54.470
traumatic event, and what it might create
after.

00:13:54.470 --> 00:13:58.470
They settled on SCP-066, Eric's Toy.

00:13:58.470 --> 00:14:04.279
First, they built the simulation around SCP-066
as it first behaved when it arrived at the

00:14:04.279 --> 00:14:05.940
SCP Foundation.

00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:11.040
The result produced was a world made of colorful
yarn, filled with living yarn creatures roaming

00:14:11.040 --> 00:14:14.920
about the landscape as Eric's Toy rolled around
among them cheerfully.

00:14:14.920 --> 00:14:20.420
Then, they input the details of the incident
that shifted the entity's behavior, when a

00:14:20.420 --> 00:14:24.220
D-Class attempted to cut off a piece of its
yarn body for study.

00:14:24.220 --> 00:14:29.190
The resulting pocket dimension was made, not
of yarn, but of fleshy tendrils dripping with

00:14:29.190 --> 00:14:34.670
red that curled and writhed like tentacles,
grasping and squeezing aggressively at anything

00:14:34.670 --> 00:14:37.201
that intruded on the space.

00:14:37.201 --> 00:14:43.540
A striking visual representation of the chance
in the anomaly's mental and emotional state.

00:14:43.540 --> 00:14:47.510
Next was SCP-1867, Lord Blackwood.

00:14:47.510 --> 00:14:52.320
Lord Blackwood's pocket out of reality was
the interior of a grand hunting lodge, with

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:58.420
a roaring fire in the fireplace and an impressive
- if a bit macabre - bear skin rug stretched

00:14:58.420 --> 00:15:00.089
across the floor.

00:15:00.089 --> 00:15:05.110
Lord Blackwood stood, in all of his brightly-colored
sea slug glory, at a bar in the corner of

00:15:05.110 --> 00:15:09.579
the room next to a glass of whiskey and a
hand-carved wooden pipe.

00:15:09.579 --> 00:15:14.740
All along the wall were various trophies,
taxidermy of a variety of wild beasts that

00:15:14.740 --> 00:15:19.930
the slug had hunted over the years, as well
as artifacts picked up along its travels:

00:15:19.930 --> 00:15:24.110
fossils, rare books, paintings, and primitive
weapons.

00:15:24.110 --> 00:15:28.009
There were also grainy old photographs of
Lord Blackwood with many of his associates

00:15:28.009 --> 00:15:32.949
from over the years, other famed hunters and
gentleman explorers he had embarked on his

00:15:32.949 --> 00:15:35.240
expeditions alongside.

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:41.440
SCP-4910, the Grinner, would dwell in a volcanic
landscape, where rock and lava were replaced

00:15:41.440 --> 00:15:46.300
with fleshy pink gums and teeth jutted out
of every available surface.

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:47.310
Gnarly.

00:15:47.310 --> 00:15:53.870
SCP-076, Able, would use his pocket dimension
as a battle arena, a grand coliseum of sorts

00:15:53.870 --> 00:15:58.819
filled with every weapon imaginable, where
he could trap his strongest would-be opponents

00:15:58.819 --> 00:16:03.411
and force them into a fight to the death.

00:16:03.411 --> 00:16:08.339
SCP-527, Mr. Fish's simulated pocket world
resembled the city of Boston, with one notable

00:16:08.339 --> 00:16:13.650
difference: every depiction of a human being,
from statues to billboard advertisements to

00:16:13.650 --> 00:16:18.110
magazine covers, showed them with fish heads
atop their human bodies.

00:16:18.110 --> 00:16:23.370
There was not a human head to be seen, except
at what would have ordinarily been the seafood

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:24.370
market.

00:16:24.370 --> 00:16:29.660
There, chests of ice held fresh human heads
ready to be sold.

00:16:29.660 --> 00:16:34.209
Though the sight of the human heads was a
bit disconcerting, the research team understood

00:16:34.209 --> 00:16:36.560
the significance of this place.

00:16:36.560 --> 00:16:40.649
It made sense that Mr. Fish would want to
retreat to a world that matched his lived

00:16:40.649 --> 00:16:44.490
experience, where everyone else looked like
him.

00:16:44.490 --> 00:16:49.610
There was even a hat shop stocked with tiny
little formal hats like his very own tophat.

00:16:49.610 --> 00:16:55.889
If SCP-2800, Cactusman, had a place between
realities that belonged exclusively to him,

00:16:55.889 --> 00:16:58.790
it would be an underground superhero hideout.

00:16:58.790 --> 00:17:03.079
The room depicted on the monitor resembled
the Bat Cave, but with all of the bats-themed

00:17:03.079 --> 00:17:06.400
decor replaced with cactus-themed items instead.

00:17:06.400 --> 00:17:11.929
There were also several large saguaro cacti
planted in pots throughout the space, as well

00:17:11.929 --> 00:17:16.800
as several Cactus Man costumes in glass cases,
ready to be worn.

00:17:16.800 --> 00:17:21.970
SCP-294, the Coffee Machine, would have a
secret world filled with every liquid substance

00:17:21.970 --> 00:17:27.209
known to man, and several still undiscovered,
floating through the air but somehow never

00:17:27.209 --> 00:17:28.940
mixing together.

00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:33.690
Any beverage anyone could ever ask for would
be there, just waiting for the right order

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:35.210
to come in.

00:17:35.210 --> 00:17:37.760
SCP-352, Baba Yaga, was next.

00:17:37.760 --> 00:17:43.220
It was a large forest, seemingly ordinary
at first glance, but within its depths lurked

00:17:43.220 --> 00:17:48.870
every fear a person could ever have, depending
on what unsuspecting victim she was able to

00:17:48.870 --> 00:17:50.470
pull into the darkness.

00:17:50.470 --> 00:17:55.250
There could be a high-up cliffside waiting
for someone afraid of heights, a giant spider

00:17:55.250 --> 00:18:01.740
awaiting an arachnophobe, or thick, inky blackness
waiting for someone afraid of the dark.

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:07.049
All around the forest floor, her hair curled
waiting to ensnare her prey.

00:18:07.049 --> 00:18:15.200
SCP-662, more specifically, SCP-662-1, Mr.
Deeds, quite possibly already occupied a pocket

00:18:15.200 --> 00:18:17.950
dimension when his bell was not in use.

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:22.049
Though they had no way to know for certain,
the simulation predicted that his break room

00:18:22.049 --> 00:18:27.400
of sorts might look like this: a blue room
with two shelves filled with cleaning tools,

00:18:27.400 --> 00:18:32.049
a brown couch, and a little bed in the corner
where the butler could sleep during his time

00:18:32.049 --> 00:18:33.299
off.

00:18:33.299 --> 00:18:39.400
SCP-169, Leviathan, would disappear into an
aquatic pocket dimension, a place large enough

00:18:39.400 --> 00:18:45.280
for it to swim comfortably, possibly forever,
in the peaceful infinite ocean.

00:18:45.280 --> 00:18:51.549
Then, the research staff decided to input
SCP-096 and see what the Shy Guy's pocket

00:18:51.549 --> 00:18:53.170
dimension might look like.

00:18:53.170 --> 00:18:58.580
Unlike the Old Man, this anomaly was not aggressive
all the time, and it seemed to take no pleasure

00:18:58.580 --> 00:18:59.710
in hunting.

00:18:59.710 --> 00:19:05.610
Instead, it acted in a kind of twisted self-defense,
attacking anything that saw its face and set

00:19:05.610 --> 00:19:09.620
it off on a spree of violence that ended in
death.

00:19:09.620 --> 00:19:14.720
SCP-096's potential pocket dimension was a
dark, dismal labyrinth, like something out

00:19:14.720 --> 00:19:17.299
of the Greek myth of the Minotaur.

00:19:17.299 --> 00:19:21.720
Stone corridors twisted this way and that,
leading any potential intruders down dead

00:19:21.720 --> 00:19:27.500
ends and away from the center, where SCP-096
hid from sight.

00:19:27.500 --> 00:19:33.570
In the center, there was light and life, trees,
grass, a small pond, and a nest filled with

00:19:33.570 --> 00:19:41.390
blind birds chirping and singing to SCP-096
as it sat in complete obscurity, away from

00:19:41.390 --> 00:19:42.390
prying eyes.

